---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InquiryForm from '../components/InquiryForm.astro';
import '../styles/services.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Business Services | Cloud & Capital" description="Understand technology costs, improve recurring reporting, and put one useful change to work. Finance-led reviews and practical setup with Diana Molski.">
  <main id="main-content" class="offer-page">
    <section class="offer-shell offer-intro" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <p class="offer-eyebrow">Finance judgment. Practical technology.</p>
      <h1 id="services-title">Know what’s worth<br /><em>doing next.</em></h1>
      <p class="offer-lede">Your technology bills keep arriving. Your reports still take too long. And apparently you’re supposed to add AI to all of it.</p>
      <p class="offer-summary">I help service businesses understand their technology costs, improve recurring reporting, and make practical changes using the tools they already have.</p>
      <div class="offer-actions"><a class="offer-button" href="#inquiry">Tell me what’s getting stuck →</a><a href="/services/examples">See example reviews</a></div>
      <p class="offer-route">Here for the markets? <a href="/learn">Explore investing &amp; trading lessons →</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="offer-shell fit-band" aria-labelledby="fit-title"><p class="offer-eyebrow">Start with a real question</p><h2 id="fit-title">A growing bill. A recurring report.<br />A process that needs babysitting.</h2><p>These services suit owners and operations leads of agencies, consultancies, and similar service businesses with a specific decision to make, records to work from, and someone who can put the result to use.</p><p>If the answer is a simple fix you can handle yourself, that’s a useful answer too.</p></section>
    <section class="offer-shell process-band" aria-labelledby="starting-point-title">
      <h2 id="starting-point-title">Where should we start?</h2>
      <div class="offer-grid">
        <div><h3>“Is this worth what we pay?”</h3><p>A renewal, overlapping subscriptions, or a bill you can’t explain.</p><a href="#technology-cost-review">Technology Cost Review →</a></div>
        <div><h3>“Why does this take so long?”</h3><p>A recurring report or task with too much copying, checking, or chasing.</p><a href="#workflow-review">AI &amp; Workflow Review →</a></div>
        <div><h3>“We know what needs building.”</h3><p>A defined reporting template, workflow, or small tool you need help putting into use.</p><a href="#practical-setup">Practical Setup →</a></div>
      </div>
      <p>Not sure—or dealing with both a bill and a workflow? <a href="#inquiry">Describe what’s happening.</a> We’ll agree a useful starting point before any paid work.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="offer-shell service-list" aria-label="Business offers">
      <article id="technology-cost-review" class="service-row">
        <div><p class="offer-eyebrow">01 · Technology Cost Review</p><h2>Know what you’re paying for.<br /><em>And what deserves a second look.</em></h2></div>
        <div><p>Bring a confusing software bill, an upcoming renewal, or a question about overlapping tools. We’ll look at cost, use, dependencies, and the work involved in changing anything.</p><p class="scope-note">One business · up to 10 software or AI subscriptions · three recent billing months, plus annual charges and renewal terms.</p><ul><li>A reconciled spending summary.</li><li>Keep, review, or change options with their assumptions.</li><li>A prioritized action list, including what needs checking.</li></ul><p>Cancellations and migrations are separate. Detailed cloud allocation, commitments, or architecture need their own FinOps scope.</p><a href="/services/examples#cost">See a fictional cost review →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article id="workflow-review" class="service-row">
        <div><p class="offer-eyebrow">02 · AI &amp; Workflow Review</p><h2>Find where the work<br /><em>gets stuck.</em></h2></div>
        <div><p>Bring the recurring task that keeps stealing your afternoon. We’ll map the steps and compare a simpler process, existing features, conventional automation, and AI.</p><p class="scope-note">One workflow · up to three tools · two or three redacted examples.</p><ul><li>A current-process map with bottlenecks and missing information.</li><li>Options with costs, checking, and maintenance considered.</li><li>One pilot outline with a success measure and a named owner.</li></ul><p>The review gives you a plan you can use independently. Building it is separately scoped.</p><a href="/services/examples#workflow">See a fictional workflow review →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article id="practical-setup" class="service-row">
        <div><p class="offer-eyebrow">03 · Practical Setup</p><h2>Put one useful<br /><em>improvement to work.</em></h2></div>
        <div><p>Once the result is clear, I can help configure a project-cost reporting template, improve an intake-to-report process, or build a small automation.</p><p class="scope-note">One agreed result · up to three compatible tools · individually quoted.</p><ul><li>A configured template, workflow, or small tool.</li><li>Checks for normal use, missing inputs, and relevant failures.</li><li>Instructions, a walkthrough, and a clear handoff.</li></ul><p>A paid review isn’t required when the setup scope is clear. New features and ongoing support are agreed separately.</p></div>
      </article>
    </section>
    <section class="offer-shell process-band" aria-labelledby="process-title"><p class="offer-eyebrow">Useful answers. A defined scope.</p><h2 id="process-title">Here’s how we work.</h2><div class="offer-grid"><div><h3>Start in writing</h3><p>Tell me the question, tools, and what happens when the process doesn’t work. We can use a call or recorded walkthrough if it helps.</p></div><div><h3>Agree the work</h3><p>You receive the scope, inputs, fixed quote, timing, and handoff terms before paid work begins.</p></div><div><h3>Get a usable result</h3><p>Receive the findings or agreed setup, with assumptions, checks, and a practical next step.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="offer-shell reviewer" aria-labelledby="reviewer-title"><div><p class="offer-eyebrow">Your reviewer &amp; builder</p><h2 id="reviewer-title">Hi, I’m Diana.</h2><p>I earned my degree in finance and worked in wealth management at Morgan Stanley. Today I bring that financial perspective to business costs, reporting, and the practical use of technology.</p><p>I built <a href="https://lens.cloudandcapital.com">AI Cost Lens</a> and <a href="https://guard.cloudandcapital.com">Cloud Cost Guard</a> to make cost evidence easier to understand. What do the numbers actually support?</p><p class="scope-note">B.S. Business Administration, Finance · FinOps Certified Practitioner · FinOps Certified FOCUS Analyst · AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner · Microsoft Azure AI Fundamentals</p></div><aside><p class="offer-eyebrow">Before you renew</p><h3>Your software deserves a little performance review.</h3><p>Eight questions to help you decide whether to keep, adjust, or investigate a subscription.</p><a href="/resources/software-renewal">Use the free checklist →</a></aside></section>
    <section class="offer-shell faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><h2 id="faq-title">A few practical questions</h2><details><summary>Do I have to buy new software?</summary><p>Existing tools and simpler processes are considered first. Any proposed external cost is made explicit.</p></details><details><summary>Is implementation included in a review?</summary><p>A review provides findings and the next step. Setup is separately scoped and quoted when useful.</p></details><details><summary>Do we need a call?</summary><p>We can begin in writing. A call or recorded walkthrough is available when helpful.</p></details><details><summary>What will it cost?</summary><p>You receive a defined scope and fixed quote before work begins. Setup fees depend on the result and systems involved.</p></details><details><summary>Are savings guaranteed?</summary><p>Findings explain evidence and assumptions. Time freed up is kept separate from cash savings; a recommendation may be to keep the existing system.</p></details></section>
    <section id="inquiry" class="offer-shell contact-band" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title"><p class="offer-eyebrow">Let’s start with the question</p><h2 id="inquiry-title">Tell me what’s getting stuck.</h2><p>A few lines are enough; you don’t need to choose a service first. Tell me what’s happening and what you’d like to change. Leave out financial records, passwords, and sensitive client information.</p><p>I’ll reply with any questions needed to understand the fit. If there’s a useful project, you’ll receive a scope and quote to review before deciding.</p><InquiryForm kind="business" /></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
